.TH BACKDROP-CONFIG 5 "2026-11-13" "backdrop 2.79.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
backdrop-config \- the configuration file of backdrop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/backdrop/config.yaml\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
backdrop reads its settings from a YAML file, by default $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/backdrop/config.yaml (~/.config/backdrop/config.yaml). A missing file is written with the defaults on the first run; keys left out take their defaults, and a key backdrop does not know is reported as a warning (backdrop status and backdrop doctor show them). A wrong value stops every command with the key named.
.PP
The running daemon follows saved changes to the file: most settings apply at once, some on the next item or playlist load, and the few that need a restart are announced in a notification. backdrop never rewrites the file except to change single keys (the menu saving a visualizer preset, the web interface's Config page), keeping comments and layout.
.PP
Durations take seconds or a unit: 90, "90s", "5m", "1h".
.SH DISPLAY
What the daemon shows and how: monitors, durations, notifications, bounce and smoothing.
.TP
\fBdisplay.monitors\fR (list of monitor names, default \fBauto\fR)
auto (every active output, from xrandr) or the outputs to use, such as DP\-1
.TP
\fBdisplay.image_duration\fR (duration, default \fB300\fR)
How long each image shows
.TP
\fBdisplay.video_duration\fR (duration, default \fB120\fR)
Wall time per video before the next; shorter videos loop whole times that fit, 0 loops each forever
.TP
\fBdisplay.video_loop\fR (choice, default \fBloop\fR, one of loop, bounce)
loop from the start, or bounce: backwards to the start, then forwards
.TP
\fBdisplay.bounce_cache_gb\fR (number, default \fB10\fR)
Room for reversed copies of bouncing videos, in GB; 0 for no limit
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth\fR (boolean, default \fBfalse\fR)
Make smooth_fps copies of slowed videos with RIFE in the background, so they play without stutter
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth_fps\fR (integer, default \fB30\fR)
Frames a second a slowed video shows once smoothed
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth_below\fR (integer, default \fB20\fR)
Smooth only slowed videos that show fewer frames a second than this; copies made before stay
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth_blend\fR (boolean, default \fBtrue\fR)
Blend frames (mpv interpolation) while a slowed video has no smoothed copy yet
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth_rife\fR (text, default \fBrife\-ncnn\-vulkan\fR)
The rife\-ncnn\-vulkan binary; its rife\-v4.6 model folder sits beside it
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth_cache_gb\fR (number, default \fB10\fR)
Room for smoothed copies of slowed videos, in GB; 0 for no limit
.TP
\fBdisplay.smooth_gpu\fR (integer, default \fB\-1\fR)
The GPU RIFE runs on (its Vulkan device number), \-1 for the CPU; a GPU job moves to the CPU on the kernel's first sign of a hang
.TP
\fBdisplay.allow_upscale\fR (boolean, default \fBfalse\fR)
Show media smaller than the monitor
.TP
\fBdisplay.order\fR (choice, default \fBrandom\fR, one of shuffle, random)
How next with filters picks a match: random (any still ahead) or shuffle (the next in order)
.TP
\fBdisplay.notify\fR (choice, default \fBcommands\fR, one of commands, all, off)
Desktop notifications: on commands, on every load, or off
.TP
\fBdisplay.xwinwrap_args\fR (list of strings, default \fB["\-b","\-s","\-st","\-sp","\-nf","\-ov","\-fdt","\-ni"]\fR)
xwinwrap arguments, one per line; \-g geometry is added per monitor
.TP
\fBdisplay.mpv_args\fR (list of strings, default \fB[]\fR)
Extra mpv options, one per line; mpv runs with \-\-no\-config
.SH LIBRARY
What is imported and where, and how long skipped items stay in the trash.
.TP
\fBlibrary.import_dirs\fR (list of strings, default \fB[]\fR)
Folders imported into the library, one per line
.TP
\fBlibrary.watch_imports\fR (boolean, default \fBtrue\fR)
Import new files in those folders as they appear
.TP
\fBlibrary.default_import_rating\fR (integer, default \fB2\fR)
Rating imported files are kept at
.TP
\fBlibrary.min_width\fR (integer, default \fB1024\fR)
Narrowest media kept, in pixels (either orientation)
.TP
\fBlibrary.min_height\fR (integer, default \fB768\fR)
Lowest media kept, in pixels (either orientation)
.TP
\fBlibrary.trash_days\fR (integer, default \fB30\fR)
Days skipped files stay in the trash; 0 keeps them
.TP
\fBlibrary.min_duration\fR (duration, default \fB5\fR)
Shortest video searches save and downloads fetch; 0 for any length. Imports are not checked
.SH MENU
backdrop menu: the rofi menus.
.TP
\fBmenu.style\fR (choice, default \fBpanel\fR, one of panel, minimal)
panel (preview, details, buttons) or minimal
.TP
\fBmenu.rofi_args\fR (list of strings, default \fB[]\fR)
Extra rofi arguments, one per line
.TP
\fBmenu.workspace\fR (i3 workspace, default \fBtrue\fR)
i3: an empty workspace while the menu is open (true: "backdrop", or a name); false to stay
.SH WEB
backdrop web: the web interface on 127.0.0.1.
.TP
\fBweb.port\fR (integer, default \fB7737\fR)
Port `backdrop web` listens on; a taken one falls back to a free port
.SH LOAD
Under system load the daemon drops to images, then stops the wallpaper and visualizers, and comes back as it falls.
.TP
\fBload.enabled\fR (boolean, default \fBfalse\fR)
Lighten the display while the system load is high
.TP
\fBload.window\fR (choice, default \fB1\fR, one of 1, 5, 15)
Load average read: over 1, 5 or 15 minutes
.TP
\fBload.image_above\fR (number, default \fB12\fR)
Load above which videos give way to images; empty for none
.TP
\fBload.off_above\fR (number, default \fB24\fR)
Load above which the wallpaper and visualizer stop; above image_above; empty for none
.TP
\fBload.resume_ratio\fR (number, default \fB0.75\fR)
A level ends once the load falls below this share of its threshold
.TP
\fBload.sustain\fR (duration, default \fB60\fR)
How long the load must stay above a threshold first
.TP
\fBload.resume_after\fR (duration, default \fB300\fR)
How long it must stay below before a level ends
.SH SCREENSAVER
backdrop screensaver: an empty i3 workspace per output with only the wallpaper and visualizers.
.TP
\fBscreensaver.idle\fR (boolean, default \fBfalse\fR)
Start the screensaver when the desktop has been idle
.TP
\fBscreensaver.idle_minutes\fR (number, default \fB10\fR)
Idle minutes before it starts
.TP
\fBscreensaver.max_load\fR (number, default \fBnull\fR)
No idle start above this load; empty for no limit
.TP
\fBscreensaver.preset\fR (text, default \fBscreensaver\fR)
Visualizer preset while it runs; empty keeps the running one
.TP
\fBscreensaver.preset_without_lyrics\fR (text, default \fBscreensaver\-instrumental\fR)
Visualizer preset while the song has no lyrics (from sleeve); empty keeps preset
.TP
\fBscreensaver.next_on_song\fR (boolean, default \fBtrue\fR)
A media player starting another song changes the wallpaper on every monitor
.TP
\fBscreensaver.hide_pointer\fR (boolean, default \fBtrue\fR)
Hide the mouse pointer while it runs
.TP
\fBscreensaver.hint\fR (boolean, default \fBtrue\fR)
Say how to leave on entering and when a key or the mouse is used (needs xprintidle)
.TP
\fBscreensaver.workspace\fR (text, default \fBbackdrop\fR)
i3 workspace it shows on
.TP
\fBscreensaver.on_enter\fR (list of strings, default \fB["polybar\-msg cmd hide"]\fR)
Command run on entering, one argument per line
.TP
\fBscreensaver.on_leave\fR (list of strings, default \fB["polybar\-msg cmd show"]\fR)
Command run on leaving, one argument per line
.TP
\fBscreensaver.sources\fR (list of strings, default \fB["rated_videos"]\fR)
Not read yet
.TP
\fBscreensaver.streams\fR (list, default \fB[]\fR)
Not read yet; a YAML list, such as \- { url: https://..., title: rain }
.SH OUTPUT
How the CLI prints on a terminal; piped output stays plain.
.TP
\fBoutput.symbols\fR (choice, default \fBauto\fR, one of auto, nerd, unicode, ascii)
Symbols in the CLI's output: auto picks by terminal
.TP
\fBoutput.progress_gradient\fR (list of colors, default \fB["#00c8ff","#a050ff"]\fR)
Progress bar colors, at least two
.SH SOURCES
API sources and their credentials. Only sites with a public API qualify.
.TP
\fBsources.pexels.api_key\fR (text, secret, default \fB""\fR)
Pexels API key (PEXELS_API in the environment also works); never shown
.TP
\fBsources.pexels.per_page\fR (integer, default \fB80\fR)
Results asked for per search page
.TP
\fBsources.pexels.image_min_size\fR (choice, default \fBlarge\fR, one of large, medium, small)
Smallest image variant considered
.SH VISUALIZER
GLava, sleeve or projectM visualizers above the wallpaper. Its keys are checked by src/visualizer/settings.js and described in docs/specs/visualizer.md; the defaults are listed here.
.TP
\fBvisualizer.enabled\fR (default \fBfalse\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.engine\fR (default \fBglava\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.monitors\fR (default \fBall\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.module\fR (default \fBbars\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.audio\fR (default \fBpulseaudio\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.source\fR (default \fBauto\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.opacity\fR (default \fB0.8\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.placement\fR (default \fBa mapping\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.bars\fR (default \fBa mapping\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.defines\fR (default \fBa mapping\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.requests\fR (default \fB[]\fR)
.TP
\fBvisualizer.glava\fR (default \fBa mapping\fR)
.SH PATHS
Where backdrop keeps its files. They default to XDG locations and are not written to the file; set one to move it.
.TP
\fBpaths.database\fR
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/backdrop/backdrop.db\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.logfile\fR
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/backdrop/backdrop.log\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.media\fR
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/backdrop/media\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.trash\fR
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/backdrop/trash\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.inbox\fR
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/backdrop/inbox\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.thumbnails\fR
\fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/backdrop/thumbnails\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.bounce\fR
\fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/backdrop/bounce\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.smooth\fR
\fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/backdrop/smooth\fR
.TP
\fBpaths.runtime\fR
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/backdrop (keep it short: mpv socket paths must fit in 107 bytes)\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbackdrop\fR(1); config.example.yaml and docs/specs/config.md in the source tree
